From: ChatGPT <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] i915: avoid RPS mutex after GT init failure

NetBSD's Linux-5.6-derived i915 GEM initialization deliberately treats
-EIO from intel_gt_init() as a wedged-GT condition where GPU submission
is disabled but KMS remains alive.  The intel_gt_init() error unwind has
already called intel_gt_pm_fini(), which destroys the RPS mutexes.

The later fbdev/KMS modeset can call intel_rps_mark_interactive().  On a
GT that failed initialization this attempts to lock the already destroyed
rps->power.mutex and can panic instead of preserving the intended KMS-only
recovery path.

Skip RPS interactive accounting only for the explicit wedged-on-init
state.  Runtime RPS behavior on successfully initialized hardware is
unchanged.

---
 sys/external/bsd/drm2/dist/drm/i915/gt/intel_rps.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/external/bsd/drm2/dist/drm/i915/gt/intel_rps.c b/sys/external/bsd/drm2/dist/drm/i915/gt/intel_rps.c
--- a/sys/external/bsd/drm2/dist/drm/i915/gt/intel_rps.c
+++ b/sys/external/bsd/drm2/dist/drm/i915/gt/intel_rps.c
@@ -650,6 +650,16 @@ static void gen6_rps_set_thresholds(struct intel_rps *rps, u8 val)
 
 void intel_rps_mark_interactive(struct intel_rps *rps, bool interactive)
 {
+	/*
+	 * intel_gt_init() may fail with -EIO after intel_gt_pm_fini() has
+	 * torn RPS down.  i915_gem_init() deliberately keeps KMS alive for
+	 * that case, so fbdev may still reach this function.  Do not touch
+	 * the destroyed RPS mutex when the GT was wedged during init.
+	 */
+	if (intel_gt_has_init_error(rps_to_gt(rps)))
+		return;
+
 	mutex_lock(&rps->power.mutex);
 	if (interactive) {
 		if (!rps->power.interactive++ && rps->active)
-- 
